{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And she took for him a basket of reed.</b> 'For him' — for his benefit and deliverance. And Yocheved his mother did a wise thing, a great stratagem: she placed him at the river's edge so that Pharaoh's astrologers would see and say that the deliverer has already been cast into the river, for they knew this through their astrology, and they would report the matter to Pharaoh, and then the decree would be annulled, for they would not investigate whether after his being cast into the river he had actually died or not, nor would they search for him. And this is what the Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted: the stargazers announce to the months what will come upon you — and not everything. And so the astrologers and seers of Pharaoh the wicked — the power of their wisdom failed, and they found no certainty in their vision — and the Holy One, blessed be He, delivers whom He wishes to deliver."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:12.410889826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}